Bottom line recommendation
- Claim the student loan interest up to $2,500 (above‑the‑line).
- Report the consulting on Schedule C; if the $780 is for that business, include it on Schedule C.
- Claim the home‑office deduction on Schedule C. The regular method (Form 8829) will likely give a much larger deduction than the simplified method given your rent — and it will reduce both income tax and SE tax.
