  - Estimated AGI ≈ $68,356.25
- Standard deduction (MFJ) = $27,700
- Estimated taxable income ≈ $68,356.25 − $27,700 = $40,656.25

6) Charitable gift
- $1,400 to St. Mary’s Food Bank is deductible only if you itemize (Schedule A). Because the standard deduction ($27,700) is larger than your likely itemized total, you will probably not deduct the $1,400 on Schedule A if you take the standard deduction. Keep the receipt in case you later itemize or records are requested.

Which forms you’ll need (federal)
- Form 1040 — main return.
- Schedule 1 — reporting interest income and adjustments (student loan interest, half of SE tax, etc.).
- Schedule C — report consulting income and business expenses (including the unreimbursed $780 and the home-office deduction you get via Form 8829).
- Schedule SE — calculate self-employment tax.
