2) Self‑employment tax and QBI
- Your net profit from Schedule C is subject to self‑employment (SE) tax (Social Security + Medicare; roughly 15.3% on net SE earnings after the 92.35% adjustment). You also get an above‑the‑line deduction equal to half of the SE tax.
- You will likely be eligible for the Qualified Business Income (QBI) deduction (IRC §199A) of up to 20% of your qualified business income from the consulting business (Form 8995 or 8995‑A) — with your income level this should not be limited by the high‑income phase‑in rules.

3) Home office (self‑employed only)
- Because you are self‑employed for the consulting income, you can claim a home office deduction if the office is used regularly and exclusively for business.
- You reported: office = 165 sq ft exclusive; home = 850 sq ft. Business-use percentage = 165 / 850 ≈ 19.41%.
