  a) Simplified method: $5.00 × 165 sq ft = $825 (no Form 8829 required). Simple and often preferable for small deductions.

  b) Actual (regular) method: allocate actual home expenses to the business. For rent: $1,600 × 12 = $19,200 annual rent; × 19.4118% ≈ $3,726 deductible as home office portion of rent (plus a similar share of utilities if you pay them separately). To claim the actual method you use Form 8829 (Expenses for Business Use of Your Home) and carry the result to Schedule C. Note: actual method gives the larger deduction here (≈$3,726 vs $825), but the home‑office deduction for the actual method can be limited by your net profit from the business — any disallowed amount may be carried forward (Form 8829 handles limits and carryovers).

