- Self-employment tax base = 92.35% × $4,392 ≈ $4,056
- Self-employment tax ≈ 15.3% × $4,056 ≈ $620
- You may deduct half of SE tax (~$310) as an adjustment to income on Schedule 1.
- Note: these are rough estimates; exact numbers depend on precisely what business expenses you include and whether you choose simplified vs regular home office.

Interest reporting
- Because total interest > $1,500, you must attach Schedule B to Form 1040. Keep 1099-INT / 1099-DIV statements from Citi and E*TRADE.

Itemize vs standard deduction
- Standard deduction MFJ 2023 = $27,700.
