  - Maximum deduction is $2,500 per year (even though you paid $2,700). You can take up to $2,500 as an adjustment to income on Form 1040 (Schedule 1), subject to MAGI phaseouts. With your income (~$75k total before adjustments) you are well below the 2023 phaseout for MFJ, so you should be able to take the full $2,500.

